[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5294070620","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/122411#issuecomment-5294070620","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122411","id":5294070620,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABO40bXA","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-14T13:50:38Z","updated_at":"2026-08-14T13:50:38Z","body":"I don't know that this is a bug, the method doesn't use the other node's unique name, it considers the unique name of the node itself:\n> returns the shortest path accounting for this node's unique name \n\nSo, with `C` and `D` having unique names, this should be what this means:\n```\n+ A\n`-+ B\n  `-+ C\n    `-+ D\n```\n```gdscript\nextends Node\n\nfunc _ready() -> void:\n\tassert(self.get_path_to(%D, true) == ^\"%C/D\")\n```","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5294070620/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laug